# Deferred work → future-fixes.md

Cassandra V2 keeps a parking lot for work that should **not** be done in the
current session:

**File:** [`docs/future-fixes.md`](docs/future-fixes.md)

## When to use it

If the user says to do something **later**, **not now**, **defer**, **park**,
**add to the todo list**, or similar — **do not implement**. Instead add a
proper new entry at the **top** of the Open items list in `docs/future-fixes.md`.

## What a proper entry includes

Follow the template of existing items:

- Short title
- Filed date, area, key files, related routines/PRs if known
- What happens today / symptom
- Why it matters
- Proposed fix (when ready)
- Risks / decisions
- Status: deferred

Enough context that a future session can pick it up without re-reading chat.

## Also

- Link stays in `docs/README.md` Guides table (`future-fixes.md`).
- Do not create parallel TODO files; use this one list.
